1) If we only connect the cables and do not configure any IP address, will PC0 be able to ping PC1:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    - PC0 has no IP address
    - PC1 has no IP address
    - Router also have no IP address

    Without IP address, there is not Layer3 communication.

    (No, PC0 cannot ping PC1 because ping uses (IP Layer3), and without IP address there is
    no source IP, no destination IP, and no routing)

    Even if both PCs are connected to the same switch, ping still requires IP address


2) How many different IP networks do you think we will need in this topology:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    PC0 ---- SW1 ---- R1 ===== R2 ---- SW2 ---- PC1

    Network 1:
    ----------
    PC0 is connected to R1
    Should PC0 and R1 be in the same IP network: YES
    so that's our first network
    Example: 192.168.10.0/24

    Network 2:
    ----------
    R1 is connected to R2
